      "writtenOn": "2025-10-23T18:02:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In theory we could avoid a temporary `result` variable by calling `Consume` before calling `_png_continue_decode`.  This seemed fragile or even incorrect - in my mind the contract of `Consume` is that it should allow `CFC_CodecMemory` to discard or shuffle around the consumed bytes (i.e. invalidating spans that have been previously returned).  So, I think the pattern in this CL is safer.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "4a4a4cc3_49b44b9b",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "core/fxcodec/png/libpng_png_decoder.cpp",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 182,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 182,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "  // A temporary variable is used here because calling codec_memory-\u003eConsume()\n  // before _png_continue_decode() could be fragile. Consume() might invalidate\n  // the buffer returned by GetUnconsumedSpan(), and _png_continue_decode()\n  // needs to access this buffer.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "89efc0542c4d2a3553602555f58aeaabf2b01d04",
