      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using `!\u003d` instead of `\u003e` means that:\n\n1. We don\u0027t have to use `first` when calling `ReadBlockAtOffset`\n2. More importantly: it means that there are no garbage bytes at the end of `codec_memory_`.  I guess `libpng` (and Rust PNG) ignore input after `IEND` PNG chunk, but having garbage bytes still seems unhygienic (it so happens that the garbage currently can only happen at the end of input when `remain_size` changes the `input_size` in the last iteration, but this kind of dependency is fragile).",
